					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213#post-4612859</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213/manifest-327:vultures#post-4612859</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2020 20:22:41 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>barredowl</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6001754</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hmm, fair enough. I can definitely see how this could be too simple or without any kind of payoff. Really, my intent here was to showcase the differences the Commission and the Foundation have and how the Commission reacted with the advent of colonialism, but if the simplicity of it distracted you from it, that's fair. Regardless, thanks for the comment!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213#post-4612855</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213/manifest-327:vultures#post-4612855</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2020 20:13:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>pamplemousse</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3456379</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I don't think there was enough of a payoff here. The witches cause trouble&#8230; the witches tell the Cargo guys that if they destroy the building it will destroy their colony&#8230; they destroy the building&#8230; and it destroys their colony. Just feels too&#8230; simple.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213#post-4611386</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13264213/manifest-327:vultures#post-4611386</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2020 00:29:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>CityToast</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1372124</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I am really happy to see the finished product of this one. I think it's particularly great because it showcases the differences between the Commission and the Foundation. The final section, where the Regents decide to destroy the Cargo, is a stark contrast the the pure &quot;contain, protect&quot; seen in the mainlist. It's a reminder that the Commission is Foundation-adjacent, but certainly not parallel.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
